<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13025" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dēmissĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				letting down, sinking, lowering</i> (very rare). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop.: storiarum, * <i><span class="en">Caes. B. C.
				2, 9, 5</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">barbae,</span>”
				<i>a letting grow</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Macr. S. 1, 22, 4</span></i>
			.—In plur.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">clipei aenei demissiones,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr.
					5, 10 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b> * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> (Acc. to demissus, <i>no.</i> II.
			A.): animi, <i>dejection</i>, * <i><span class="en">Cic. Tusc.
				3, 7, 14</span></i>. —* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> In medic. lang., <i>an
				abatement, mitigation</i> (opp. accessio), Coel. Aur. Acut. 1,
			4.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
